        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add package changelog previews for plugin publishing",
        "body": "Closes #1288.\n\nAdds README-based package changelog previews for plugin release publishes and guards the async preview path so stale generated text cannot overwrite user edits. Package changelog preview now verifies the caller can publish/manage the existing package before reading previous release storage; direct owners, publisher org members, moderators, and admins are allowed, while unrelated signed-in users are denied before storage is read.\n\nBehavior proof:\n```text\nHead: 0c6c02c51e49\n\nReal local-auth browser run:\n- Disposable local Convex seeded a package with prior README-backed releases.\n- Chromium opened the real /plugins/publish release flow and uploaded a new package folder.\n- The changelog textarea auto-filled from package history:\n  \"- added 3 file(s).\\n- Updated README and package contents.\"\n- After editing the textarea to \"Manual release notes after preview.\", the manual text remained after the field settled.\nResult: 1 passed (chromium).\n\nFocused regression proof:\n- Denied existing-package preview throws before release storage is read; storage.get was not called.\n- Direct owner, publisher org owner/admin/publisher, platform admin, and platform moderator access paths pass.\n- Delayed route preview cannot overwrite a manually edited changelog.\nResult: 11 targeted tests passed; changed test-file set also passed with 3 files / 316 tests.\n```\n\nCI state: GitHub Actions checks on this head are green for packages, e2e-http, static, types-build, unit, Playwright local-auth, CodeQL, CodeQL Light, secret scan, and pr-gates. The remaining Vercel status is the OpenClaw Foundation team authorization gate, not a source/test failure.\n",
